     "topic": "e-cigarettes-and-tobacco",
     "level": "city",
     "rule": "Daejeon Metropolitan City can designate outdoor places as smoke-free under the National Health Promotion Act. The ordinance lists the kinds of place it can cover: city parks and riverside walking paths, among other places. The exact designated sites are set by notice and marked by signs, so follow the signs. The fine is KRW 50,000 (about A$53.13, RBA rate of 30 October 2026, A$1 = KRW 941.07).",
